<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBP-AG19-F001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBP-AG19-F001" ;
  triage:title "Ambiguous SendRequest.to placeholder semantics -- no type-level signal distinguishing intended recipients from placeholder/self values" ;
  triage:description "rust-best-practices-agent finding from AG19-REAL-QA-1: SendRequest.to (crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs) is a plain `pub to: AgentAddress` field, and AgentAddress itself (crates/atm-core/src/address.rs:11-14) is a plain struct { agent: AgentName, team: Option<TeamName> } with no enum/newtype variant distinguishing an intended real recipient from a placeholder or self-referential value. In the ack-reply path (crates/atm-core/src/ack/mod.rs), prepare_ack_reply_with_runtime constructs the outbound SendRequest by string-formatting the resolved reply_target into `to: format!(\"{}@{}\", reply_target.agent, reply_target.team).parse()?` -- the same untyped AgentAddress is used whether the value is a genuinely external recipient or a self-referential/placeholder target, so callers cannot distinguish the two cases at the type level and must rely on out-of-band convention. Confirmed identical struct shape and identical ack-path construction on all 8 ordered feature branches (pAG-s18 through pAG-s25) and on integrate/phase-AG; the finding is open everywhere, not fixed on any branch." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AG" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:category "rust-best-practices" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-19T18:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RBP-AG19-F001/pAG-s18/1> ;
