  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/integrate/65593144> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s25/c245c2ea> ;
  triage:notes "INITIAL_PASS. No prior canonical record existed for this finding_id. Sweep pattern: `struct SendRequest` and `to: format!(` in crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs and crates/atm-core/src/ack/mod.rs across all 9 supplied worktrees. Repeatable pattern confirmed present in identical form on every branch: SendRequest.to is `pub to: AgentAddress`, and AgentAddress is an untyped struct { agent, team } with no RecipientKind-style enum or PlaceholderAddress/RealAddress newtype distinction. Because the defect is a shared-crate struct definition rather than branch-specific code, it is open uniformly and is NOT fixed_partial. highest_open_branch is the latest feature branch in the ordered promotion list (feature/pAG-s25-live-two-daemon-proof, order_index 8), not integrate/phase-AG (order_index 9) -- per standing project convention, fix dispatch targets the latest sprint branch and never the integration branch directly; merge-forward will close the occurrence on lower/earlier branches. integrate/phase-AG is recorded as openOn for correlation completeness only and is explicitly not selected as promote_to_branch, consistent with the task note that integrate's current tip does not yet include AG.19's fix (i.e. integrate is behind the feature-branch line, not ahead of it). Full sweep_scope=file_only repeatable sweep was executed on promote_to_branch (feature/pAG-s25-live-two-daemon-proof) across the two originally implicated files; no additional occurrences beyond the two recorded were found in that branch's send/mod.rs or ack/mod.rs." .

